-- title:
--   Vanishing of H¹ at the archimedean slot for odd p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime with $p \neq 2$, let $S$ be a finite set of rational primes, and let $M$ be a representation of the absolute Galois group $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ (realised as the group of field automorphisms of `AlgebraicClosure ℚ` over $\mathbb{Q}$) on a $\mathbb{Z}/p$-vector space that is finite-dimensional over $\mathbb{Z}/p$; let $u$ be the unique element of `Unit`. The family `extArithLoc S` is indexed by `extArithIndex S` $=$ `Unit` $\oplus$ $S$: at an index `Sum.inr q` it is the homomorphism `primeLocalToGlobal q` from the local Galois group at $q$ into the global group, while at the archimedean index `Sum.inl u` the local group is the subgroup `archimedeanDecomposition` generated by complex conjugation and the homomorphism is `archimedeanLoc`, the inclusion of that subgroup. The assertion is that the $\mathbb{Z}/p$-dimension of $H^1$ of the restriction of $M$ along this archimedean inclusion, i.e. of $H^1(\langle c \rangle, M)$ for $c$ complex conjugation, is zero.
--
--   This is the archimedean term in the local computation underlying the Greenberg–Wiles style Euler-characteristic count: at an infinite place the first cohomology of the decomposition group, of order dividing $2$, vanishes in odd residue characteristic. It is used in the construction of global cohomology classes with prescribed local restrictions, namely by [`groupCohomology.exists_mem_continuousH1S_locRes_eq_of_forall_sum_theta_eq_zero_arch_of_ne_two`](thm.html#groupCohomology.exists_mem_continuousH1S_locRes_eq_of_forall_sum_theta_eq_zero_arch_of_ne_two).
